    "reading_order": 3,
    "text": "In general, given a composite number x, we factorise it as x = p1p2 ... pn, where\np1, p2,..., pn are primes and written in ascending order, i.e., p1  p2\n . . .  pn. If we combine the same primes, we will get powers of primes. For example,",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
